I didn't pull the prod data. Auto mode blocked the scan of `erp-customers-prod`, and the repo's DynamoDB notes also mark prod resource-table queries as interactive only. I haven't tried any other way to read it.

I wrote the script for you to run yourself:

```
! cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-harshanandiwada-workspace-pii-redactor/fcd0cbe5-57d3-44cd-be0b-5b20d34eb5d1/scratchpad && uv run --project /Users/harshanandiwada/workspace/pii-redactor python3 business_customers.py 10
```

It's read-only. It scans up to 10 pages (about 10 MB) of the table, keeps only rows where `is_individual` is false, and flags a row when:
- the `name` looks like a person (two or three capitalized words, no company words like Inc, LLC, Co or Store, no digits, `&` or `@`);
- the email is at a consumer domain (gmail, yahoo, icloud and so on);
- the shipping or billing address `full_name` is the same as `name`.

It prints the counts, then up to 8 rows that hit more than one rule and 4 that hit one. Each line shows the connection id, the row id, a masked name (`J*** S****`) and the email domain, so the real names don't end up here.

The tests are written and pass. They aren't committed:
- **`test/utils/redact_resources_pii_test.py`**: every resource test now goes through the resource itself (`Order`, `CartOrder`, `ErpSalesOrder`, `ErpCustomer`, `ErpEmployee`), using a fixture that sets up a flagged org. New `ErpCustomer` cases cover:
  - an individual, fully redacted;
  - a business, left unchanged;
  - `is_individual` set to `None` or `IntegrationNotImplemented`, left unchanged;
  - an empty row, as the webhook diff passes for a new customer;
  - a page with one individual and one business;
  - an unflagged org.
- **`test/utils/boto_test.py`**: `test_get_rows_for_dynamo_webhook_stores_new_erp_customer` runs a new customer through the webhook diff, the case that crashed before.

`yarn test utils -k "get_rows_for_dynamo_webhook or redact_resources_pii"` gives 37 passed. Your change to `resources/erp/customers.py` is still unstaged along with them.

